00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:17.010
Under the Employee.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:19.610
As Hans sat beneath a balustrade of
Hitotsubashi, his editor called out to him.

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:20.440
"Congratulations.  Your work will be serialized."

00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:23.680
He had been recognized as a diligent author by the other authors, but the staff had mocked him as third-rate.

00:23:23.680 --> 00:23:25.850
Were he to serve the company diligently, perhaps he would be able to attain the same status as the staff...

00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:26.650
This was a lie.

00:23:26.650 --> 00:23:28.890
No matter how he persevered, he was, after all, just a
hireling. Writing comics remained nothing but temporary work.

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:29.920
No matter how hard he struggled, he was below the staff.

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:32.020
"This is keeping you from burning out, isn't it.
Without it, you'd be crushed beneath the staff."

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:33.290
The master called out to Hans in a kind voice, and Hans replied.

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:35.690
"Don't act like I'm like you, you fourth-rate."
The master was beneath he who was beneath the staff.

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.930
Illustration:
Oomori Hidetoshi

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.930
Let's despair over the next volume too!
